{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fresh reproduction on current origin/main (2026-08-10): two normal bug closes durably reached status=closed, then the post-close `metrics.blame._find_fixing_commit -> _resolves_to -> resolve_ticket_id` scan treated historical four-character commit subjects as ticket references. It emitted successive ambiguous-prefix errors for `b2bb`, `28f9`, `a9dd`, `dbb2`, and `3e8b` and kept scanning instead of terminating promptly. This is a sibling of the reported enrichment-drain symptom: the shared unsafe assumption is that an unqualified four-hex fragment is a resolvable ticket reference. The affected surface here is optional caused-by derivation after the close event, not enrichment queue reduction. The durable closes were unaffected; the local post-write process required interruption after status confirmation."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786386334493141001,"uuid":"c8d1ae26-c0b0-4d53-85b5-fd9b203001fa"}